Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:35:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] Add Gemini 3.8 Flash high profiles for both harnesses

Published Gemini 3.8 Flash high runs are tagged
`google-gemini-3-8-flash-high` and
`google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-provider-adapter`, but neither profile is
checked in; only the low Provider Adapter profile is.

- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high: manual_rolling on the Gemini
  Interactions API, MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH 175k, carry-forward instruction on.
  Its request block matches the Provider Adapter profile (store=false,
  thinking_summaries=auto, 65,536 max output tokens), so the two profiles
  differ only in harness settings; summaries are recorded but not replayed.
- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-provider-adapter: the low Provider Adapter
  profile with thinking_level=high (harness_summary compaction at 175k,
  8,192-token summary cap, 1,048,576 context).

These are reconstructions; they are not confirmed to match the settings
ARC used for the published runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
